---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
---
<SiteLayout title="Getting started - Open MindMap" description="Install and integrate the Open MindMap modular React runtime.">
  <div class="shell docs-layout">
    <aside class="docs-sidebar" aria-label="Documentation navigation">
      <span>Overview</span><a href="/docs/">Introduction</a><a class="is-active" href="/docs/getting-started/">Getting started</a>
      <span>Steps</span><a href="#install">Install</a><a href="#choose">Choose a runtime</a><a href="#extend">Add features</a><a href="#stream">Stream AI output</a>
    </aside>
    <article class="docs-content">
      <span class="eyebrow">Getting started</span><h1 id="getting-started">From install to interactive map in three minutes.</h1>
      <p>The new package entries are intentionally explicit. Select the behavior your surface needs, import the matching stylesheet, and add extensions or editor features only when requirements justify them.</p>

      <h2 id="install">1. Install</h2>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>pnpm add @xiangfa/mindmap</code></pre></div>
      <p>React and ReactDOM are peer dependencies. KaTeX is optional and only required by the LaTeX extension.</p>

      <h2 id="choose">2. Choose a runtime</h2>
      <h3>Read-only and interactive</h3>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> {'{'} <span class="fn">MindMapViewer</span> {'}'} <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/viewer'</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/viewer.css'</span>

<span class="kw">const</span> markdown = <span class="str">`Product strategy
- Market
  - Research
  - Positioning
- Delivery
  - Prototype
  - Measure`</span>

<span class="kw">export function</span> <span class="fn">StrategyMap</span>() {'{'}
  <span class="kw">return</span> &lt;<span class="tag">MindMapViewer</span> <span class="prop">markdown</span>={'{markdown}'} <span class="prop">selectable</span> /&gt;
{'}'}</code></pre></div>
      <h3>Editable</h3>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> {'{'} <span class="fn">MindMapEditor</span> {'}'} <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/editor'</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/editor.css'</span>

&lt;<span class="tag">MindMapEditor</span> <span class="prop">markdown</span>={'{markdown}'} /&gt;</code></pre></div>

      <h2 id="extend">3. Add only the features you use</h2>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> {'{'} <span class="fn">historyFeature</span> {'}'} <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/features/history'</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> {'{'} <span class="fn">searchFeature</span> {'}'} <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/features/search'</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/features/history.css'</span>
<span class="kw">import</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/styles/features/search.css'</span>

<span class="kw">const</span> features = [<span class="fn">historyFeature</span>(), <span class="fn">searchFeature</span>()]

&lt;<span class="tag">MindMapEditor</span>
  <span class="prop">markdown</span>={'{markdown}'}
  <span class="prop">features</span>={'{features}' }
/&gt;</code></pre></div>
      <p>Keep Feature and Extension arrays at module scope, or memoize them with <code>useMemo</code>, so editor sessions keep stable identities between renders.</p>

      <h2 id="stream">4. Stream model output</h2>
      <p>The headless core exposes a Markdown stream controller. Append delta chunks as they arrive; subscribers receive coalesced document and patch updates.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> {'{'} <span class="fn">createMarkdownStream</span> {'}'} <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="str">'@xiangfa/mindmap/core'</span>

<span class="kw">const</span> stream = <span class="fn">createMarkdownStream</span>()
stream.<span class="fn">subscribe</span>((update) =&gt; {'{'}
  console.<span class="fn">log</span>(update.document, update.patches)
{'}'})

<span class="kw">for await</span> (<span class="kw">const</span> chunk <span class="kw">of</span> response.body) {'{'}
  stream.<span class="fn">append</span>(decoder.decode(chunk, {'{'} stream: true {'}'}))
{'}'}</code></pre></div>
      <div class="docs-callout">Use the Viewer for model output unless users must edit the generated structure. Read-only is now a separate dependency boundary rather than a runtime boolean on the full editor.</div>

      <h2 id="features">5. Compose editor features</h2>
      <p>History, search, import, export, Markdown editing, and AI are separate Features. Each consumes the same Editor controller, so the application does not need a second tree or history stack.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; historyFeature &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/history'
import &#123; searchFeature &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/search'
import &#123; importFeature &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/import'
import &#123; exportFeature &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/export'
import &#123; markdownEditorFeature &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/features/markdown-editor'

const features = [
  historyFeature(),
  searchFeature(),
  importFeature(),
  exportFeature(),
  markdownEditorFeature(),
]

&lt;MindMapEditor markdown=&#123;markdown&#125; features=&#123;features&#125; /&gt;</code></pre></div>
      <p>Import the matching Feature stylesheet for the controls you mount. Add <a href="/docs/ai/">AI generation</a> when the host has a generator or provider proxy.</p>

      <h2 id="interactions">6. Persist changes and control the view</h2>
      <p>Use Document callbacks for persistence and viewport callbacks for presentation state. Refs expose commands without making the host maintain a duplicate Document.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; useRef &#125; from 'react'
import type &#123; MindMapEditorRef &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/editor'

const editorRef = useRef&lt;MindMapEditorRef&gt;(null)

&lt;MindMapEditor
  ref=&#123;editorRef&#125;
  markdown=&#123;markdown&#125;
  onMarkdownChange=&#123;setMarkdown&#125;
  onDocumentChange=&#123;(document) =&gt; saveDocument(document)&#125;
  onViewportChange=&#123;(viewport) =&gt; rememberViewport(viewport)&#125;
/&gt;

editorRef.current?.fitView()
editorRef.current?.focusNode('mm-0-0')</code></pre></div>
      <p>The Editor ref also provides <code>getDocument</code>, <code>getController</code>, node commands, folding, history, SVG export, outline export, and Markdown access. See the <a href="/docs/api/#refs">full ref table</a> for the exact methods.</p>

      <h2 id="localization">7. Localize the editor</h2>
      <p>When <code>locale</code> is omitted, the runtime detects English or Simplified Chinese from the browser. Pass a locale for a fixed language, or override only the strings your application needs.</p>
      <div class="code-block"><pre><code>import &#123; MindMapEditor &#125; from '@xiangfa/mindmap/editor'

&lt;MindMapEditor
  markdown=&#123;markdown&#125;
  locale="en-US"
  messages=&#123;&#123;
    newNode: 'New idea',
    source: 'Markdown source',
  &#125;&#125;
/&gt;</code></pre></div>
      <div class="docs-callout">Continue with the <a href="/docs/syntax/">syntax guide</a>, <a href="/docs/ai/">AI guide</a>, <a href="/docs/styling/">styling guide</a>, and <a href="/docs/api/">API reference</a>.</div>
    </article>
    <aside class="docs-toc" aria-label="On this page"><span>On this page</span><a href="#install">Install</a><a href="#choose">Choose a runtime</a><a href="#extend">Add features</a><a href="#stream">Stream output</a><a href="#features">Compose features</a><a href="#interactions">Persist changes</a><a href="#localization">Localization</a></aside>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
